From 089f03bc449102ec7cdb41e882c1eb2068e43938 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 11:58:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] perf: cut retained memory per reactive text/attr binding
 and component

- StaticHost.collectInnerHost / StaticArrayHost.render no longer clone
  pathContext (plus a LinkedNode) for atom/function children: text
  bindings never consume hostPath, so AtomHost/FunctionHost now share
  the parent's context and carry a small {owner, elementPath,
  debugSource} position object instead; FunctionHost materializes the
  full child context lazily (childPathContext) only when the function
  renders structural content, producing a chain identical to before
- reactive attribute bindings become ReactiveAttributeEffect (fields on
  the effect) instead of LightBindingEffect + a 6-capture closure and
  its Context (~50B less per binding, one less indirection on trigger)
- StaticHost.collectRefHandles/collectDetachStyledChildren only assign
  when the element actually has handles: unconditional undefined writes
  pushed every element host beyond its in-object slots, costing a
  ~20B PropertyArray per host (every list row paid it)
- ComponentHost: name becomes a getter on type; ref/__this props are
  assigned only when present; inputProps is swapped for the shared
  empty object after render so the JSX call-site props object can be
  collected (components never rerender)

All 601 browser tests + 6 node tests pass; typecheck output unchanged.
