From e5f798041c1277a2ca967ac4e87a4cf9950fa245 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 12:14:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] perf: store single reactive child/attr binding without
 wrapper arrays

- StaticHost.reactiveHosts/attrEffects accept a single Host/effect
  directly when an element has exactly one reactive child or attribute
  (the typical list-row shape), saving an array header + elements store
  per row; iteration goes through renderReactiveHosts/
  destroyReactiveHosts/destroyAttrEffects helpers
- attrEffects is also no longer allocated when every unhandled attr is
  a prop:/hBHcprefixed config key
- effects are registered on the host before their initial run so a
  throwing first evaluation (no root error hook) can still be
  unsubscribed on destroy
- tests touching the internal reactiveHosts shape updated
